      "content": "\"During the pre-flight check for flight AS442, an anomaly was detected in Engine 1, characterized by a fluctuation in the fuel flow sensor, resulting in error code E-104. Subsequent checks revealed oscillation in pressure, leading to the detection of error code E-202. A secondary cooling system inspection indicated a variance in sensor E-405, although no immediate fault was found. Despite the pilot's request for a manual override, the E-104 subsystem remained unresponsive. Maintenance was logged for sensor calibration error, identified as E-303. Further investigation into the E-104 subsystem revealed potential issues with the fuel flow control valve, which may have contributed to the initial fluctuation. Additionally, the E-202 error code may be linked to a malfunctioning pressure regulator, necessitating further diagnostic tests. The E-405 sensor variance could be attributed to a calibration drift in the secondary cooling system, warranting a comprehensive sensor recalibration. These findings highlight the need for a thorough inspection of the E-104 subsystem, pressure regulator, and secondary cooling system sensors to prevent future anomalies during pre-flight checks.\"",
